* Reference 4: an inline comment is the substring between `/*` and `*/`, it
* stands between lexical units, and the compiler ignores it. The line-comment
* half of the clause is exercised by every fixture that opens with `*`; this one
* is the inline half, and it puts the comment in all three positions a comment
* can take -- before the pattern, between the pattern and the result, and inside
* a call -- because a comment that is dropped in one position and not another is
* the failure this fixture is for.
$EXTERN Prout;

$ENTRY Go {
  /* before the pattern */
  e.X /* between the pattern and the result */ = <Prout /* inside a call */ 'block-comment-ok'>;
};
